{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>It is not like the land of Egypt.</b> But rather it is better than it, and this promise was spoken to Israel at their departure from Egypt, for they were saying: perhaps we will not come to a land as good and fine as this one. Could it be that Scripture speaks of its inferiority, and thus He said to them 'It is not like the land of Egypt' but rather worse than it? Scripture says: ״וְחֶבְרוֹן שֶׁבַע שָׁנִים נִבְנְתָה לִפְנֵי״ etc. (Numbers 13) — one man built it: Ham built Zoan for Mitzrayim his son, and Hebron for Canaan. The way of the world: a man builds the fine one first and afterward builds the inferior one, for the refuse of the first he puts into the second, and everywhere the more beloved comes first. From this you learn that Hebron is finer than Zoan. And Egypt is praised above all lands, as it is said (Genesis 13) ״כְּגַן ה׳ כְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם״, and Zoan is the praise of Egypt, for it is the seat of kingship, as it says (Isaiah 30) ״כִּי הָיוּ בְצֹעַן שָׂרָיו״. And Hebron was the refuse of Israel — therefore they set it aside for a burial-place of the dead; and even so, it is finer than Zoan. And in Ketubot (112a) they expounded the matter differently: is it possible that a man builds a house for his younger son and afterward for his older son? Rather, it was built upon one of the seven of Zoan." "<b>From which you came out.</b> Even the land of Rameses in which you dwelled — and it is the best of the land of Egypt, as it is said ״בְּמֵיטַב הָאָרֶץ״ etc. (Genesis 47) — even it is not like the land of Israel." "<b>And you water it with your foot.</b> The land of Egypt needed to bring water from the Nile with your foot and to water it — you needed to disturb your sleep and toil, and the low place drinks and not the high, and you raise the water from the low to the high. But this one — <b>it drinks water from the rain of heaven</b> — you are asleep on your bed and the Holy One, blessed be He, waters low and high, what is seen and what is not seen, all at once (Sifrei)." "<b>Like a vegetable garden.</b> Which does not suffice with rain, and they water it by foot and by shoulder."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:36.385329578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}